9
00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:31.857
What you will build:

10
00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:34.527
Ask Grocery, the platform's assistant.

11
00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:54.369
Customers ask about policies (how long does a refund take?), products (is SKU-AMU48213 in stock?), recipes (what do I need for rajma chawal?) and their own orders (where is order A123456?), and the assistant can act: track, cancel, refund.

12
00:00:54.649 --> 00:01:09.988
It is the design ChatGPT for X / design a RAG system interview question, done as a production system: retrieval quality, GPU serving economics, cost controls, and agents that cannot be talked into moving money.

13
00:01:11.338 --> 00:01:16.927
The four labs (all deterministic; what is real and what is simulated is stated in each):

14
00:01:17.207 --> 00:01:20.557
L1: retrieval (real algorithms, toy embeddings).

15
00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:36.901
With hybrid search, the complete answer reaches the prompt for 67% of questions with 25-word chunks, 93% with 120-word chunks and 98% with 400-word chunks, at 1.8x the prompt tokens.

16
00:01:37.181 --> 00:01:46.674
BM25 misses 45% of paraphrased questions; embeddings miss every SKU code; reciprocal rank fusion covers both.

17
00:01:46.954 --> 00:01:50.410
L2: serving (real schedulers, simulated GPU).

18
00:01:50.690 --> 00:02:00.759
The same 8B model on one GPU: one request at a time, or static batches of 16, never meet a 2 s time-to-first-token p99;.

19
00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:22.952
continuous batching that reserves the 16k context window per request serves 2 req per second (90 GPUs for the 180 req per second dinner peak);. paged KV memory serves 7 req per second (26 GPUs); adding a prefix cache for the shared system prompt, 9 req per second (20 GPUs).

20
00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:26.944
L3: cost controls (real policies, simulated traffic).

21
00:02:27.224 --> 00:02:40.643
A semantic cache serves wrong answers for 22 to 40% of questions at every threshold from 0.6 to 0.99: another customer's order number is 0.99 similar.

22
00:02:41.993 --> 00:02:46.302
A cache keyed by intent + entities, never sharing personal answers:

23
00:02:46.582 --> 00:02:48.907
62% hits, 0 wrong.

24
00:02:49.187 --> 00:02:59.683
Small-model routing with escalation: $0.96 per 1,000 answers versus $8.10 all-large, at the same quality.

25
00:02:59.963 --> 00:03:03.654
L4: agents (real policy layer, simulated model).

26
00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:16.755
In 20,000 conversations a naive agent takes 527 unauthorized actions, acts on 398 other customers' orders and pays 135 double refunds.

27
00:03:17.035 --> 00:03:23.051
Idempotency keys, argument checks, an intent allow-list and confirmation take each to 0.

28
00:03:23.331 --> 00:03:24.313
Reading time:

29
