4.5M times ~3,000 about 13.5B input + 1B output tokens.

147
00:11:34.531 --> 00:11:35.598
Self-hosted:

148
00:11:35.878 --> 00:11:40.123
20 to 90 GPUs at peak depending on the scheduler (L2).

149
00:11:40.403 --> 00:11:41.747
Provider API:

150
00:11:42.027 --> 00:11:49.750
14.5B tokens per day times list price: compare with L2's GPU cost per 1,000 answers.

151
00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:59.911
The input tokens dominate, which is why chunk size (L1), prefix caching (L2) and caching whole answers (L3) are the big levers.

152
00:12:01.261 --> 00:12:03.970
Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG).

153
00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:13.615
The model's weights don't contain your policies, prices or this customer's orders, and fine-tuning them in is slow, costly and can't be updated per minute.

154
00:12:13.895 --> 00:12:18.567
RAG retrieves the relevant text at question time and puts it in the prompt:

155
00:12:18.847 --> 00:12:25.951
Ingest: split documents into chunks, embed each chunk, index both the text (BM25) and the vectors.

156
00:12:26.231 --> 00:12:29.431
Retrieve: for each question, find the top-k chunks.

157
00:12:29.711 --> 00:12:36.965
Generate: prompt = instructions + retrieved chunks + question; the model answers from them and cites them.

158
00:12:38.315 --> 00:12:40.213
Chunk size is the first trade-off.

159
